# Performance

## Bundle Budget

| Chunk | Limit (raw) | Limit (gzip) | Current |
|-------|-------------|--------------|---------|
| `index` (main) | 400 KB | 130 KB | 400 KB / 125 KB |
| Page chunk (each) | 350 KB | 90 KB | ChatPage 345 KB / 86 KB |
| Vendor chunk | 100 KB | 30 KB | Radix 81 KB / 27 KB |
| CSS | 50 KB | 10 KB | 27 KB / 6 KB |

Vite warns at `> 400 KB` (raw) per chunk. If a chunk grows — decompose via `React.lazy` or `manualChunks`.

## Code Rules

### Lazy Loading

All page-level components — React.lazy:

```typescript
const DraftsPage = React.lazy(() =>
  import("~/pages/drafts").then((m) => ({ default: m.DraftsPage })),
);
```

Heavy libraries — dynamic import:

```typescript
const EmojiPicker = React.lazy(() => import("emoji-picker-react"));
```

### Zustand Selectors

Subscribe to the minimum:

```typescript
// ✅ Single field — re-render only when loading changes
const loading = useStore((s) => s.loading);

// ❌ Entire store — re-render on any change
const store = useStore();
```

For derived data — functions outside the component:

```typescript
// ✅ selector computes outside render
const unreadCount = useStore((s) => s.drafts.filter((d) => !d.read).length);
```

### Memoization

Only when actually needed:

```typescript
// ✅ Filtering a large list
const filtered = useMemo(() => items.filter(predicate), [items, predicate]);

// ✅ Callback passed to child component
const handleClick = useCallback(() => doSomething(id), [id]);

// ❌ Don't memoize simple computations
const fullName = `${first} ${last}`;  // no useMemo
```

### Lists

- `key` — stable ID (not index)
- Long lists (>100 items) — virtualization (react-virtuoso)
- `React.memo()` for item components in lists

### Images

- `loading="lazy"` on images outside viewport
- Dimensions in attributes (`width`, `height`) to prevent layout shift
- Avatars: fixed sizes via Tailwind (`w-10 h-10`)

### Event Handlers

```typescript
// ❌ Inline function in map — recreated on every render
{items.map(item => <Item onClick={() => handleClick(item.id)} />)}

// ✅ Pass id, handler inside Item
{items.map(item => <Item key={item.id} id={item.id} onClick={handleClick} />)}
```

### Effects

```typescript
// ✅ Cleanup subscriptions
useEffect(() => {
  const unsub = subscribe();
  return () => unsub();
}, []);

// ❌ Leak — no cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  subscribe();
}, []);
```

## Performance Monitoring

### API call timing

```typescript
import { perf } from "~/shared/lib/perf";

const end = perf.startTimer("api:fetchMessages");
const data = await fetchMessages();
end();  // auto-warning if >1s
```

### Web Vitals

```typescript
import { perf } from "~/shared/lib/perf";

// In main.tsx — once
perf.reportWebVitals();
// Logs LCP, FID, CLS, Long Tasks → logger
```

### App startup

```typescript
perf.mark("app:init");
// ... init code
perf.mark("app:ready");
perf.measure("app:startup", "app:init", "app:ready");
```

## Thresholds

| Metric | Target | Action if exceeded |
|--------|--------|-------------------|
| LCP | < 2.5s | Optimize initial render, lazy load |
| FID | < 100ms | Reduce main thread work |
| CLS | < 0.1 | Set image dimensions, no layout shifts |
| API response | < 1s | Show skeleton, `perf` warns in log |
| Long task | < 50ms | Break into microtasks |
| Bundle chunk | < 400KB | Split with React.lazy |
| Zustand selectors | 1 field | Minimize re-renders |

## Render Performance Anti-Patterns (CRITICAL)

These patterns were found and fixed during the project audit. Each one caused cascading re-renders affecting the entire UI. **Do NOT reintroduce them.**

### Anti-Pattern 1: Zustand getter returning new array/object

```typescript
// ❌ CRITICAL: creates new array on EVERY subscription check
// Triggers re-render of every component that calls streams()
streams: () => Array.from(streamsMap.values()).sort(...)

// ✅ FIXED: cache by Map reference, return same array if Map hasn't changed
let cachedRef: Map<...> | null = null;
let cachedResult: StreamWithLast[] = [];
streams: () => {
  const map = get().streamsMap;
  if (map !== cachedRef) {
    cachedRef = map;
    cachedResult = Array.from(map.values()).sort(...);
  }
  return cachedResult;
}
```

**Rule: Zustand getters that derive data (sort, filter, map) MUST cache by input reference.**

### Anti-Pattern 2: React.memo missing on list items

```tsx
// ❌ MessageBubble renders 100+ times in a chat — without memo, ALL re-render when parent updates
export const MessageBubble: React.FC<Props> = ({ message }) => { ... };

// ✅ Wrapped in React.memo — only re-renders when its own props change
export const MessageBubble = React.memo<Props>(({ message }) => { ... });
```

**Rule: Components rendered in a list (`.map()`) MUST be wrapped in `React.memo`.**

### Anti-Pattern 3: Empty array constant as selector result

```tsx
// ❌ Returns [] (new empty array) — new reference on every render
const participants = useCallStore((s) => s.getParticipants(roomId));
// getParticipants: return rooms.get(id) ?? [];  ← new [] every time!

// ✅ Module-level constant for empty fallback
const EMPTY: Participant[] = [];
// getParticipants: return rooms.get(id) ?? EMPTY;
```

**Rule: Never return `[]`, `{}`, or `new Map()` as fallback in selectors/getters. Use a module-level constant.**

### Anti-Pattern 4: Inline objects/functions in JSX

```tsx
// ❌ New function + new object on every render → child re-renders needlessly
<TopBar
  onOpenProfile={() => setProfileDrawerOpen(true)}
  style={{ padding: 8 }}
/>

// ✅ Stable references
const openProfile = useCallback(() => setProfileDrawerOpen(true), []);
const style = useMemo(() => ({ padding: 8 }), []);
<TopBar onOpenProfile={openProfile} style={style} />
```

**Rule: Functions and objects passed as props to child components MUST be memoized with `useCallback`/`useMemo`.**

### Anti-Pattern 5: Expensive computation in render body

```tsx
// ❌ Sorts + groups on EVERY render (O(n log n) per render)
const groups = messages.reduce((acc, msg) => { /* group by date */ }, []);

// ✅ Memoized — only recalculates when messages change
const groups = useMemo(() =>
  messages.reduce((acc, msg) => { /* group by date */ }, []),
  [messages]
);
```

**Rule: `.sort()`, `.filter()`, `.reduce()`, `.map()` on arrays with >10 items MUST be inside `useMemo`.**

### Anti-Pattern 6: Zustand selector returning multiple fields as object

```tsx
// ❌ Creates new object on every store update → always re-renders
const { activityOpen, setActivityOpen } = useSidebarConfigStore();

// ✅ Separate selectors — only re-renders when the specific field changes
const activityOpen = useSidebarConfigStore((s) => s.activityOpen);
const setActivityOpen = useSidebarConfigStore((s) => s.setActivityOpen);
```

**Rule: Never destructure from `useStore()` without a selector. Always use individual `(s) => s.field` selectors.**

## Performance Checklist (for AI Agent)

### Every new component:
- [ ] List items wrapped in `React.memo`
- [ ] Callbacks passed to children wrapped in `useCallback`
- [ ] Objects/arrays passed as props wrapped in `useMemo`
- [ ] Zustand selectors use `(s) => s.singleField`, not destructuring

### Every new store getter:
- [ ] If it derives data (sort/filter/map), cache by input reference
- [ ] Never return `[]`, `{}`, `new Map()` as default — use module-level constant
- [ ] Getters are pure (no side effects)

### Every new page/widget:
- [ ] Page component loaded via `React.lazy()`
- [ ] Heavy libs (emoji picker, Jitsi) loaded via dynamic `import()`
- [ ] Lists >50 items use virtualization (react-virtuoso)
- [ ] Images have `loading="lazy"` and explicit dimensions
- [ ] API calls wrapped in `perf.startTimer()`

### Pre-merge check:
- [ ] `npm run build` → no chunks > 400KB
- [ ] React DevTools Profiler → no unnecessary re-renders
- [ ] Chrome DevTools Performance → no long tasks > 50ms
